WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:08.057
Dashboards put your work and your numbers side by side: open tickets, today’s schedule, sales, and data from your other tools.

2
00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:16.472
Each kind of widget has its own look. Big numbers fill their card, bars stand out, and every widget has its own color.

3
00:00:16.933 --> 00:00:23.419
To add one, click Add widget. It takes three steps. First, say what you want to see, and click Find the data.

4
00:00:23.867 --> 00:00:31.269
AI finds the data, from tickets or any tool you can use, and shows what it understood. The preview counts what matches.

5
00:00:31.733 --> 00:00:35.531
Next, choose how to show it. The AI’s pick is marked Suggested.

6
00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:40.959
Last, the details: the title, what to count, how to split it, and the width. Then add it.

7
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:46.733
Every widget has a menu, to duplicate it, or copy it to another dashboard or report.

8
00:00:47.733 --> 00:00:55.627
Or describe a whole dashboard, and AI builds it, with a preview before anything is saved. Explain tells you what the numbers say.

9
00:00:56.067 --> 00:01:06.413
Keep a dashboard private, share it with a team, or with everyone. People only see numbers they’re allowed to see. Archived projects stay available, to report on past work.

